Let $k$ be a field, let $R^\Lambda$ be the cyclotomic KLR algebra of [[def-cyclotomic-klr-quotient-at-a-dominant-weight]] on a symmetrizable Cartan datum with no imaginary simple roots, and keep the grading of [[def-klr-grading-and-diagrammatic-composition]]. Then for every $\beta\in Q_+$:
(a) every $x_a$ is nilpotent on $R^\Lambda(\beta)$, there is a monic polynomial $g_a(u)\in k[u]$ with $g_a(x_a)=0$ in $R^\Lambda(\beta)$, and $R^\Lambda(\beta)$ is a finite-dimensional graded $k$-algebra; moreover $R^\Lambda(\beta+k\alpha_i)=0$ for $k\gg0$;
(b) $R^\Lambda(\beta)$ is a graded Frobenius algebra: there is a nonzero homogeneous $k$-linear functional
$$\tau^\Lambda_\beta:R^\Lambda(\beta)\to k$$
of even degree $t^\Lambda(\beta)$, the closing-diagram functional (close the right boundary of a diagram and read the scalar in $R^\Lambda(0)=k$), which kills no nonzero left ideal, and after the symmetry adjustment of the source it is cyclic, $\tau^\Lambda_\beta(ab)=\tau^\Lambda_\beta(ba)$ for all $a,b$;
(c) consequently, for the $\#$ duality defined by $M^\#:=\mathrm{HOM}_k(M,k)^\psi$ with the descended generator-fixing anti-involution $\psi$, every finitely generated graded projective $P$ satisfies $P^\#\cong P\{t^\Lambda(\beta)\}$; the duality is a contravariant, shift-reversing equivalence on finite-dimensional graded modules which preserves projectives and sends indecomposables to indecomposables, and its duality shift on the shift orbit of any indecomposable is even, so the self-dual normalization recorded below is well defined. The rank-one computation gives $R^\Lambda(\alpha_i)\cong k[x_1]/(a^\Lambda_i(x_1))$ with $\deg x_1=2d_i$ and $t^\Lambda(\alpha_i)=2d_i(\lambda_i-1)$ in the standard choice.

Let $R=\bigoplus_\beta R(\beta)$ be a KLR algebra on a symmetrizable Cartan datum with no imaginary simple roots ([[def-quiver-hecke-klr-algebra-for-a-symmetrizable-cartan-datum]]) and let $E_i$ denote restriction $e(\beta,i)(-)$ and $F_i$, $\bar F_i$ the right-append and left-append inductions of [[def-klr-induction-and-restriction-bimodules]] (so that $\bar F_i(M)=R(\beta+\alpha_i)e(i,\beta)\otimes_{R(\beta)}M$ with $e(i,\beta)=\sum_{\nu\in I^\beta}e(i\ast\nu)$). Let $t_i$ be an indeterminate of degree $(\alpha_i\mid\alpha_i)=2d_i$. Then:
(a) for $i\ne j$ there are natural isomorphisms $E_iF_j\cong q^{-(\alpha_i\mid\alpha_j)}F_jE_i$ and $\bar F_jE_i\cong E_i\bar F_j$;
(b) for $i=j$ there is a natural isomorphism $E_iF_i\cong q^{-(\alpha_i\mid\alpha_i)}F_iE_i\oplus(\mathrm{Id}\otimes_kk[t_i])$, where $(\mathrm{Id}\otimes_kk[t_i])(M)=M\otimes_kk[t_i]$ with $t_i$ homogeneous of degree $2d_i$;
(c) the $(R(\beta+\alpha_i),R(\beta))$-bimodule kernel of $F_i$ sits in a functorial exact sequence in $\mathrm{Mod}(R(\beta))$
$$0\longrightarrow \bar F_iE_iM\longrightarrow E_iF_iM\longrightarrow q^{-(\alpha_i\mid\beta)}M\otimes_kk[t_i]\longrightarrow 0,$$
where $\otimes_kk[t_i]$ is understood in the graded sense. Equivalently, there is an exact sequence of $(R(n),R(n))$-bimodules $0\to R(n)\otimes_{R_1(n-1)}R_1(n)\to R(n+1)\to R(n)\otimes_k k[t]\to0$ in the notation of the source, with the bimodule structures induced by the embeddings $\xi_n$. All shifts are computed in the fixed grading of [[def-klr-grading-and-diagrammatic-composition]]; the functors are exact ([[thm-klr-induction-and-restriction-are-biadjoint-and-preserve-projectives]]).

Let $R^\Lambda$ be the cyclotomic KLR algebra of [[def-cyclotomic-klr-quotient-at-a-dominant-weight]], and let $E^\Lambda_i,F^\Lambda_i$ be the functors of [[def-cyclotomic-klr-induction-and-restriction-functors]]. For every $i\in I$ and $\beta\in Q_+$:
(a) the bimodule $R^\Lambda(\beta+\alpha_i)e(\beta,i)$ is a projective right $R^\Lambda(\beta)$-module, and $e(\beta,i)R^\Lambda(\beta+\alpha_i)$ is a projective left $R^\Lambda(\beta)$-module;
(b) consequently $E^\Lambda_i$ and $F^\Lambda_i$ are exact and send finitely generated graded projectives to finitely generated graded projectives; moreover $F^\Lambda_i$ preserves all projectives and $E^\Lambda_i$ preserves finitely generated ones;
(c) there is a functorial exact sequence in $\mathrm{Mod}(R^\Lambda(\beta))$
$$0\longrightarrow q^{(\alpha_i\mid 2\Lambda-\beta)}\bar F_iM\longrightarrow F_iM\longrightarrow F^\Lambda_iM\longrightarrow 0,\qquad M\in\mathrm{Mod}(R^\Lambda(\beta)),$$
where $F_i$ is the right-append and $\bar F_i$ the left-append generic induction of [[lem-generic-klr-induction-and-restriction-mixed-relations]], regarded on $R^\Lambda$-modules through the quotient, and the exponent is the Cartan pairing $(\alpha_i\mid 2\Lambda-\beta)=2(\alpha_i\mid\Lambda)-(\alpha_i\mid\beta)$ ([[def-quantum-integers-factorials-and-divided-powers-at-q-i]] records the normalization of the powers of $q$).

Let $V=\bigoplus_{\mu\in P}V_\mu$ be a $P$-graded type-one quantum weight module over $U_q(\mathfrak g)$ with its chosen label grading ([[def-quantum-weight-module-and-integrability]]), on which $E_i$ and $F_i$ act as homogeneous operators of weights $\alpha_i$ and $-\alpha_i$, and assume:
(a) the mixed relations $[E_i,F_j]=\delta_{ij}\,(K_i-K_i^{-1})/(q_i-q_i^{-1})$ hold on all of $V$;
(b) $E_i$ and $F_i$ are locally nilpotent for every $i$;
(c) every vector lies in a finite direct sum of label-weight spaces (finite support).
Then the torus action together with the operators $E_i,F_i$ extends uniquely to a $U_q(\mathfrak g)$-module structure on $V$, and $V$ is integrable; if in addition each $V_\mu$ is finite-dimensional, then the standard $i$-string decomposition of [[thm-unique-kashiwara-i-string-decomposition]] applies and $V$ is the direct sum of its finite-dimensional integrable submodules.

Let $k$ be a field, let $R^\Lambda$ be the cyclotomic KLR algebra of [[def-cyclotomic-klr-quotient-at-a-dominant-weight]], and let $\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)=\bigoplus_\beta\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda(\beta))$ be the finitely generated graded projectives and $\mathrm{Rep}(R^\Lambda)=\bigoplus_\beta\mathrm{Rep}(R^\Lambda(\beta))$ the graded modules finite-dimensional over $k$. Write $A=\mathbb Z[q,q^{-1}]$ and let $[\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)]$, $[\mathrm{Rep}(R^\Lambda)]$ be the split and abelian Grothendieck groups with their $A$-module structure ([[def-graded-grothendieck-group-shift-module-and-cartan-map]]). Then the exact functors $E^\Lambda_i,F^\Lambda_i$ (exact by [[thm-cyclotomic-klr-induction-is-projective-on-the-right]]) induce $A$-linear endomorphisms, and the normalized operators used below are
$$\text{on }[\mathrm{Proj}]:\quad F_i:=F^\Lambda_i\ \text{on }[\mathrm{Proj}(\beta)],\qquad E_i:=q_i^{1-\langle h_i,\Lambda-\beta\rangle}E^\Lambda_i\ \text{on the component }[\mathrm{Proj}(\beta+\alpha_i)]\to[\mathrm{Proj}(\beta)];$$ $$\text{on }[\mathrm{Rep}]:\quad E_i:=E^\Lambda_i,\qquad F_i:=q_i^{1-\langle h_i,\Lambda-\beta\rangle}F^\Lambda_i\ \text{on the component }[\mathrm{Rep}(\beta)]\to[\mathrm{Rep}(\beta+\alpha_i)],$$
with $K_i$ acting on both by $q_i^{\langle h_i,\Lambda-\beta\rangle}$. Then:
(a) $[E_i,F_j]=\delta_{ij}(K_i-K_i^{-1})/(q_i-q_i^{-1})$ on both Grothendieck groups;
(b) $E_i$ and $F_i$ are locally nilpotent on both, and both Grothendieck groups are $P$-graded with weight $\Lambda-\beta$ in degree $\beta$;
(c) after extending scalars to $\mathbb Q(q)$, both $[\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)]\otimes_A\mathbb Q(q)$ and $[\mathrm{Rep}(R^\Lambda)]\otimes_A\mathbb Q(q)$ are integrable $U_q(\mathfrak g)$-modules ([[lem-mixed-relations-and-local-nilpotence-give-an-integrable-quantum-action]]);
(d) the pairing $\langle[P],[M]\rangle_\beta:=\mathrm{gdim}_k(P^\psi\otimes_{R^\Lambda(\beta)}M)$ with the anti-involution of [[def-the-klr-cartan-pairing]] is well defined and nondegenerate, and under it $E_i|[\mathrm{Proj}]$ is adjoint to $F_i|[\mathrm{Rep}]$ and $F_i|[\mathrm{Proj}]$ to $E_i|[\mathrm{Rep}]$ ([[thm-adjoint-exact-functors-induce-adjoint-grothendieck-operators]], [[thm-projective-hom-pairing-is-additive-and-graded-sesquilinear]]).

Keep the hypotheses and the normalized operators of [[thm-cyclotomic-klr-functors-define-an-integrable-quantum-action-on-k-zero-and-g-zero]] and the vacuum $1_\Lambda$ of [[lem-the-vacuum-projective-is-a-highest-weight-generator]], and let $V_A(\Lambda)=U_A(\mathfrak g)v_\Lambda$ be the $A$-form of the integrable highest weight module of highest weight $\Lambda$ generated by $v_\Lambda$ inside the divided-power integral form $U_A$ of [[def-lusztig-divided-power-integral-form]] ([[thm-integrable-quantum-highest-weight-module-exists-and-is-unique]], [[def-quantum-verma-module-and-simple-highest-weight-quotient]]). Then:
(a) the assignment $[1_\Lambda]\mapsto v_\Lambda$ extends uniquely to an isomorphism of $A$-modules
$$\phi:[\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)]\longrightarrow V_A(\Lambda),\qquad \phi\bigl(F_i^{(n)}x\bigr)=F_i^{(n)}\phi(x)\ \ (x\in[\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)]),$$
where $F_i^{(n)}$ on the left is the induction by the divided-power projective classes of [[def-divided-power-klr-idempotents-and-projectives]] and on the right the Lusztig divided power in $U_A$;
(b) the kernel of the natural $A$-linear surjection $U_A(\mathfrak g)\twoheadrightarrow[\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)]$, $u\mapsto u\,[1_\Lambda]$, is the left ideal $\sum_i U_A(\mathfrak g)F_i^{(\lambda_i+1)}$; equivalently $\phi$ is the induced map from $V_A(\Lambda)=U_A(\mathfrak g)/\sum_iU_A(\mathfrak g)F_i^{(\lambda_i+1)}$;
(c) $\phi$ intertwines the operators $E_i,F_i,K_i$ of the two sides, so $[\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)]$ and $V_A(\Lambda)$ are isomorphic as $U_A(\mathfrak g)$-modules, and $[\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)]$ is a free $A$-module. Injectivity of $\phi$ is also obtained from the nondegeneracy of the Cartan/Shapovalov pairing: the pullback of the KLR Cartan pairing along the categorification $\gamma$ of [[thm-klr-categorification-of-the-negative-quantum-half]] agrees with the Lusztig form ([[thm-klr-cartan-pairing-agrees-with-lusztigs-bilinear-form]], [[def-the-klr-cartan-pairing]]), whose radical is exactly the annihilator ideal of (b).

Keep the field hypotheses of [[thm-cyclotomic-klr-module-g-zero-is-the-dual-integral-highest-weight-module]] and the self-dual normalization of [[def-cyclotomic-klr-diagram-duality-and-graded-module-duals]]. Let $\mathcal B_\Lambda$ be the set of classes of self-dual simple $R^\Lambda$-modules, with weight $\mathrm{wt}(S):=\Lambda-\beta$ for $S$ of weight $\beta$, and for $i\in I$ and $S$ self-dual simple put $\varepsilon_i(S):=\max\{k\ge0:(E^\Lambda_i)^k(S)\ne0\}$, $\varphi_i(S):=\varepsilon_i(S)+\langle h_i,\Lambda-\mathrm{wt}(S)\rangle$, and let $\tilde e_i[S]$ be the class of the unique self-dual simple summand of the socle of $E^\Lambda_iS$ when $\varepsilon_i(S)>0$ (one copy of the repeated simple), while $\tilde e_i[S]:=0$ when $\varepsilon_i(S)=0$; let $\tilde f_i[S]$ be the class of the unique self-dual simple module $N$ with $\tilde e_i[N]=[S]$, equivalently the self-dual simple quotient appearing in the head of the $i$-induction of $S$. Then:
(a) $(\mathcal B_\Lambda,\mathrm{wt},\varepsilon_i,\varphi_i,\tilde e_i,\tilde f_i)$ is a crystal, and there is a unique isomorphism of crystals $\mathcal B_\Lambda\to B(\Lambda)$ sending the vacuum $[k]$ to the highest weight vector, where $B(\Lambda)$ is the highest weight crystal of [[def-kashiwara-lattices-lambda-and-infinity]], [[def-crystal-graph-epsilon-phi-and-weight]] and [[thm-the-highest-weight-crystal-b-lambda-exists]];
(b) the same graph is realized by the self-dual indecomposable projective classes: under the perfect pairing of [[thm-cyclotomic-klr-module-g-zero-is-the-dual-integral-highest-weight-module]] the projective classes are dual to the simple classes, and the dual crystal operators on them agree with the operators transported from the integral highest weight module of [[thm-cyclotomic-klr-projective-k-zero-is-the-integral-highest-weight-module]]; hence the simple and projective crystals are both canonically $B(\Lambda)$.

Take $I=\{i\}$ with $(\alpha_i\mid\alpha_i)=2$, $d_i=1$, $\Lambda=2\Lambda_1$, so the cyclotomic relations are $x_1^2e(\nu)=0$. The block $R^\Lambda(2\alpha_i)$ is the quotient of $NH_2$ by $x_1^2=0$, and the self-dual simple modules are $S_0=k$ in weight $0$, $S_1=k[x_1]/(x_1)=k$ in weight $\alpha_i$ and $S_2=k$ in weight $2\alpha_i$ with $x_1,x_2$ acting by $0$. Then:
(a) $[\mathrm{Proj}(R^\Lambda)]\cong V_A(2\Lambda_1)$, with $[1_\Lambda]\mapsto v_{2\Lambda_1}$, the divided-power class $[P_{i,1}]\mapsto F_i v_{2\Lambda_1}$, the divided-power class $[P_{i,2}]\mapsto F_i^{(2)}v_{2\Lambda_1}$, and the word class $[R^\Lambda(2\alpha_i)]=(q+q^{-1})[P_{i,2}]\mapsto F_i^2v_{2\Lambda_1}$; 
(b) with the self-dual normalization, the self-dual indecomposable projectives in weights $0,1,2$ have classes $1_\Lambda$, $[P_{i,1}]$, $[P_{i,2}]$ and the Cartan pairing values against the simple classes are $\langle 1_\Lambda,S_0\rangle=1$, $\langle[P_{i,1}],S_1\rangle=1$, $\langle[P_{i,2}],S_2\rangle=1$, all other pairings $0$; equivalently $[R^\Lambda(\alpha_i)]=[S_1]$ and $[R^\Lambda(2\alpha_i)]=(1+q^2)[S_2]$ in $[\mathrm{Rep}(R^\Lambda)]$.
